{"base_rate":0.09630606860158311,"brier":0.0580131926121372,"bss":0.3334208179182082,"bss_hi":0.43812929175651977,"bss_lo":0.2247986400188719,"chart":{"base":[145.3,154.1],"fp":[218.4,175.8],"lead":"62,264.2 272,246.4 482,209.8 692,145","note":{"base":"skill 0.33 — higher than 62% of cities","fp":"low end +0pp, high end +21pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 72% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 0%; promised 39% → rained 42%"},"rel":"62,466 85.2,451.1 306.4,284"},"country":"MX","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.007572559366754628,"ess":477.7267251089666,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Ciudad Juarez</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Ciudad Juarez rain forecast is moderately skilful, and its stated probabilities are honest throughout.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (57%), believe about\n<b>61%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 758 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nEL PASO 8.5 SSE, 9.8 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.33, ranked 81 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(40&ndash;141) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>425</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>91</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>6%</td><td class='num'><b>6%</b></td><td class='num'>83</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>20%</td><td class='num'><b>24%</b></td><td class='num'>80</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>57%</td><td class='num'><b>61%</b></td><td class='num'>79</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">0 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Ciudad Juarez</b> <span class=\"muted\">Mexico</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;10% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 10% of days.</p><p>The forecast did better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">probabilities honest throughout</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.33</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>40&ndash;141\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>758 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Ciudad Juarez &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis